			"notes": "- Game tests carry signals down copper the way a player builds it.\n- Reading a redstone signal checks for copper before anything else, so blocks that are not copper cost nothing extra.\n- A copper signal remembered in one dimension is no longer read back in another, or in a later tick.\n- A copper network too big to walk warns at most once a minute, and wire beside copper is traced once per read, not once per touching block.\n- A door or water beside unpowered copper no longer walks the whole network and wakes every block along it, and a powered network wakes only the blocks that listen.\n- The note on copper's block-change hook says which changes it can miss."
		},
